    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Hysteria is the fourth studio album by The Human League, released in 1984 on Virgin Records. Built on polished synth-pop and electronic textures, it arrived after the massive success of Dare and reflected a more elaborate, high-pressure production process, with Hugh Padgham and Chris Thomas among the producers. The album’s sleek sound and crisp arrangements kept the band firmly in the pop mainstream while retaining the group’s distinctive blend of cool electronic precision and emotive melody.\n\nCommercially, Hysteria reached No. 3 on the UK Albums Chart and was certified Gold in the UK, supported by singles including “The Lebanon,” “Life on Your Own,” and “Louise.” While often overshadowed by Dare, it has since been recognized as a strong late-period Human League record, notable for its polished songwriting and ambitious production.",
